    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "COMPARISONS\n\nComparison nodes are pure: they compare two numbers and output a boolean (true / false).\nEquals, Not Equals, Greater Than, Less Than, Greater Equal and Less Equal compare whole\nnumbers; Is Between and Nearly Equal compare decimals (Nearly Equal takes a tolerance, because\ndecimals should rarely be compared with exact equality).",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          190.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "Eight comparisons stored in bool variables. Expected: equal true, different false, greater true, less false, at-least true, at-most false, between true, close true (0.1 + 0.2 is not exactly 0.3, but it is nearly equal).",
